<!--
    repipe round 5, need variadic-prototype-still-drops (crackme
    65acadf3eef082e477ff5ede, ObfuscationFiesta.exe, sub_140002530): an
    explicitly asserted variadic prototype still rendered
    sub_140001180(out,size,"%s%s",v38) - one value for two conversions - while
    the disassembly stores the missing pointer to [RSP+0x20] immediately before
    the call.  The same call spelled with five FIXED parameters recovered all
    five, so the value was live and the stack slot was reachable.

    Root cause (P6 local-alias gather, consumed by P4 trial scoring).
    AliasChecker::gatherAdditiveBase walks the stack pointer's def/use graph and
    records an escape site at the frame offset of every NON-additive use.
    MSVC's /GS prologue mixes the stack pointer into the frame cookie:

        sub  rsp,0x940
        mov  rax,qword ptr [__security_cookie]
        xor  rax,rsp                      ; RSP used as a VALUE
        mov  qword ptr [rsp+0x930],rax

    `xor rax,rsp` is not additive, so the raw stack pointer becomes an escape
    site at the BOTTOM of the frame - the shallowest offset there is.
    hasLocalAlias then answers yes for every stack location in the function, and
    checkInputTrialUse (fspec.cc:5616) scores every outgoing-argument slot
    no-use: its CALL input is replaced with constant 0 and the argument's
    computation is dead-code eliminated.  Every stack-passed argument at every
    call site in a /GS function is dropped.  GCC/Clang read the cookie from
    %fs:0x28 and never touch the stack pointer, which is why the defect is
    invisible on ELF corpora.

    Stage model: P6 "alias-facets".  The P0 assertion
    `option cookiescramble on|off` (default ON) decides whether an INT_XOR of a
    stack-pointer-derived Varnode records an escape site.

    Witness, hand-assembled to the /GS shape (SysV x86-64 so the last two of
    eight arguments are stack-passed, plus the `xor %rsp` cookie mix):

        callee:  mov 8(%rsp),%rax ; add 16(%rsp),%rax ; add rdi..r9 ; ret
        caller:  sub    $0x38,%rsp
                 movabs $0x123456789abcdef0,%rax
                 xor    %rsp,%rax              ; the cookie mix
                 mov    %rax,0x28(%rsp)
                 mov    %rdi,(%rsp)            ; argument 7
                 mov    %rsi,0x8(%rsp)         ; argument 8
                 mov    $1,%edi ... mov $5,%r8d
                 call   callee
                 mov    0x28(%rsp),%rcx ; xor %rsp,%rcx ; add %rcx,%rax
                 add    $0x38,%rsp ; ret

    Pass 1 (option cookiescramble off) reproduces the bug: the call truncates at
    the six register arguments and the two argument stores survive as dead
    assignments to stack locals.  Pass 2 (option cookiescramble on, the default)
    proves the fix: both stack-passed arguments are recovered.
-->
